--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.3-beta.1 — responsive PadBridge control panel
+
+- Kept the existing on-console and browser-based control panel as the single GUI for PS5, phone, tablet, and desktop use.
+- Fixed controller-card grid sizing so connected-controller cards shrink to the available viewport instead of forcing horizontal overflow on narrow phones.
+- Added compact small-screen spacing and header wrapping for phone-sized displays.
+- Fixed the host `make demo` target to link the math library required by its simulated live controller animation.
+- No Bluetooth, HID, paddle mapping, profile storage, or PS5 runtime behavior changed.
+- Host tests, parser fuzz tests, and browser-side JavaScript syntax checks are required before release; real PS5 / Elite Series 2 testing remains outstanding.
+
 ## 0.3.3-beta — game-state protocol verification and test reliability
 
 - Expanded the game-state client test from an unavailable-daemon smoke test to a local TCP protocol fixture: validates the request packet, decodes the v1 response fields, and rejects non-zero status and unsupported protocol versions.
